From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] task: report the instruction share beside the time share

iet_InsnUsage exists (see the etask.h patch) but nothing could read it,
and a number nobody can read is not a measurement. TaskTag_InsnUsage
answers it exactly as TaskTag_CPUUsage answers iet_CpuUsage, and reads
zero on every target that does not fill it -- which is every target whose
CPU is not translated.
---
diff --git a/rom/task/QueryTaskTagList.c b/rom/task/QueryTaskTagList.c
index b8fadf618a..bce2f341f9 100644
--- a/rom/task/QueryTaskTagList.c
+++ b/rom/task/QueryTaskTagList.c
@@ -168,6 +168,14 @@
                     *(ULONG *)(Tag->ti_Data) = 0;
             }
             break;
+        case(TaskTag_InsnUsage):
+            {
+                if (task_et)
+                    *(ULONG *)(Tag->ti_Data) = task_et->iet_InsnUsage;
+                else
+                    *(ULONG *)(Tag->ti_Data) = 0;
+            }
+            break;
         case(TaskTag_StartTime):
             {
                 struct timeval *storeval = (struct timeval *)Tag->ti_Data;
diff --git a/rom/task/task.h b/rom/task/task.h
index ead2724673..216e66f363 100644
--- a/rom/task/task.h
+++ b/rom/task/task.h
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #define TaskTag_CPUTime                 (TAG_USER + 0x00000003) // Amount of CPU time spent running
 #define TaskTag_StartTime               (TAG_USER + 0x00000004) // Time the task was started
 #define TaskTag_CPUUsage                (TAG_USER + 0x00000005) // CPU Usage of this task
+#define TaskTag_InsnUsage               (TAG_USER + 0x00000006) // Share of guest instructions, where the CPU is translated
 #define TaskTag_REG_PC                  (TAG_USER + 0x00000020)
 #define TaskTag_REG_SP                  (TAG_USER + 0x00000021)
 #define TaskTag_REG_GeneralCount        (TAG_USER + 0x00000030)
